# INTEGRATION PHASE

After acquisition, systems must pass through controlled integration:

---

## Phase 1 — Isolation

External system is sandboxed and evaluated independently.

---

## Phase 2 — Compatibility Mapping

System interfaces are mapped to CommandCenter architecture.

---

## Phase 3 — Controlled Integration

Incremental connection to existing systems under monitoring.

---

## Phase 4 — Validation

Integration is tested for:

* stability
* performance
* security
* governance compliance

---

## Phase 5 — Full Adoption

System becomes part of operational ecosystem if all validation criteria are met.

---

# RISK MANAGEMENT

All acquisitions must address:

* dependency lock-in risk
* data sovereignty risks
* operational continuity risks
* integration failure risks
* hidden technical debt risks

Mitigation strategies must be defined prior to acquisition approval.

---

# GOVERNANCE

Acquisition shall never:

* bypass validation processes (Series 704–705)
* introduce uncontrolled production dependencies
* override system architecture constraints
* violate governance rules (Series 000)
* compromise system security or integrity

Acquisition is subject to full governance enforcement.

